1
00:00:01,046 --> 00:00:03,113
Something happens to a company you own.

2
00:00:03,647 --> 00:00:04,541
Does it matter?

3
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:08,779
Rulial Markets turns that question into a landscape you can explore.

4
00:00:10,463 --> 00:00:11,984
Start with real history.

5
00:00:12,239 --> 00:00:13,969
Three hundred twenty-nine events.

6
00:00:14,155 --> 00:00:15,211
Ten companies.

7
00:00:15,676 --> 00:00:21,202
Retrieve comparable shocks, using only price windows that end before the scenario's cutoff.

8
00:00:22,817 --> 00:00:24,999
Imagine a Boeing fleet-grounding shock.

9
00:00:25,162 --> 00:00:31,373
The engine resamples historical returns into two thousand possible outcomes over five trading days.

10
00:00:31,838 --> 00:00:34,368
You see a range, with its evidence attached.

11
00:00:35,983 --> 00:00:37,747
But there is a deeper uncertainty.

12
00:00:37,968 --> 00:00:40,290
What if the rules inside your model are wrong?

13
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:42,659
Pull it apart.

14
00:00:43,193 --> 00:00:49,288
Change which analogs count, how they are grouped, the drift assumption, and how returns are resampled.

15
00:00:49,822 --> 00:00:52,330
Now run one hundred forty-four combinations.

16
00:00:54,339 --> 00:00:55,140
Same event.

17
00:00:55,268 --> 00:00:56,301
Different rules.

18
00:00:56,940 --> 00:01:03,453
In this stored example, the simulated fraction of down outcomes ranges from twenty-five to eighty-two percent.

19
00:01:03,917 --> 00:01:07,063
A confident-looking answer can depend on an assumption.

20
00:01:08,678 --> 00:01:10,233
So we ask what survives.

21
00:01:10,698 --> 00:01:15,876
Downside tail risk appears in one hundred thirty-seven of the one hundred forty-four models.

22
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:19,788
Directional agreement stays below our ninety-percent threshold.

23
00:01:21,403 --> 00:01:24,341
This is a small, hand-chosen map of model risk.

24
00:01:24,805 --> 00:01:26,012
Rulial Markets.

25
00:01:26,651 --> 00:01:28,044
Explore what could happen.

26
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,378
See what survives changing the rules.
